# scDEAL

This directory contains the scripts used to run scDEAL in the benchmark.

## Required scDEAL Files

The `data/` and `scDEALenv/` directories required by scDEAL are provided separately through the `scDrugBenchmark_env` archive because of their large size.

Download `scDrugBenchmark_env` from Zenodo:

**Zenodo:** [ ]

After extraction, locate:

```text
scDrugBenchmark_env/
└── scDEAL/
    └── scDEAL/
        ├── data/
        └── scDEALenv/
```

Copy both directories into the corresponding scDEAL directory in the GitHub repository:

```bash
cp -r scDrugBenchmark_env/scDEAL/scDEAL/data \
      scDrugBenchmark_github/methods/scDEAL/scDEAL/

cp -r scDrugBenchmark_env/scDEAL/scDEAL/scDEALenv \
      scDrugBenchmark_github/methods/scDEAL/scDEAL/
```

After copying, the directory should contain:

```text
scDrugBenchmark_github/
└── methods/
    └── scDEAL/
        └── scDEAL/
            ├── data/
            ├── scDEALenv/
            └── [benchmark-related scDEAL source files]
```

This step must be completed before setting up the Docker environment and running scDEAL.

## Prepare Example Inputs

scDEAL uses raw count matrices and metadata files as input.

From the `data/` directory of the GitHub repository, run:

```bash
Rscript prepare_scdeal_example.R
```

The prepared inputs are saved under:

```text
data/example/
├── balanced_1000/scdeal_input/
├── imbalanced_1_3/scdeal_input/
└── imbalanced_1_30/scdeal_input/
```

## Docker Environment

scDEAL uses the shared Python Docker environment in:

```text
methods/shared_main_env/
```

Build the image from `methods/shared_main_env/`:

```bash
sudo docker build -t scdrugbenchmark-main .
```

Start the container from the root directory of the `scDrugBenchmark_github` repository:

```bash
sudo docker run --rm -it \
-v "$(pwd)":/workspace \
scdrugbenchmark-main
```

Inside the container, navigate to scDEAL:

```bash
cd /workspace/methods/scDEAL
```

Then follow the commands in the Run section below.

## Run the Example

From the `methods/scDEAL/` directory, run:

```bash
PYTHON_EXEC=/path/to/python ./run_scdeal_example.sh
```

The script evaluates the following parameter combinations:

```text
Bottleneck: 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512
Sampling: upsampling, downsampling, SMOTE
```

## Output

Predictions are saved to:

```text
example_output/
```